(r'''An envoy STOPPED or ROBBED by a body (an attributed T3 outcome; never CAUGHT by BD's own act) is an OUTRAGE: the envoy's court gains a GRIEVANCE and a CASUS on the LANDED grievance ladder against whoever HARBOURS or SPONSORS the body (§10.2 (a)'s `peace_unkept` patch AIMED at the harbourer — or at the sponsor once the tie has leaked, §10.4 — and GR's demand road; never a second ladder), and its court's stance fork turns the body `hunted` with its BOUNTY fork opened (§9.9, §9.11).''',
r'''An envoy STOPPED or ROBBED by a body (an attributed T3 outcome; never CAUGHT by BD's own act) is an OUTRAGE — and it reaches the envoy's court AS A TELLING, NEVER AS THE ATTRIBUTION'S TRUTH [CURED 2026-10-20 (fp-final P5) — P5C-15 · WC-BD-55 (RULINGS-P5 C.15): the court decided its hunt, its bounty and its casus on `bodyOnRoute` — the TRUTH of which body (Law One)]: BD's word step (§2.7 step 8) writes the attributed outcome's rumor entry with the typed `bodyId` slot (§2.4) at the hop's WITNESS settlements and the rumor road carries it on (`hopDelayTicks`; the robbed envoy, home again, among its carriers); from the week the court HAS HEARD it, its forks read `believedBodyOf(worldState, courtId, bodyId)` — whom it believes struck: the envoy's court gains a GRIEVANCE and a CASUS on the LANDED grievance ladder against whoever it believes HARBOURS the body (a court's `harboured` stance is a public fact) or SPONSORS it (once the tie has LEAKED, §10.4) — §10.2 (a)'s `peace_unkept` patch AIMED at that harbourer or sponsor, and GR's demand road; never a second ladder — and its stance fork turns the body `hunted` with its BOUNTY fork opened (§9.9, §9.11); the ATTRIBUTION itself (`bodyOnRoute`) stays TRUTH for the receipt and the DM's scrutiny (who in fact). A NAMELESS body carries no `bodyId` slot (BD23): its outrage reaches the court as the brigandage it feeds — no named fork and no bounty.'''),
